---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const storage = `<data_path>/
  <dataset-name>/
    data_df.parquet
    raw_data/
    embeddings/
      <dataset>_<model-short-name>.npz
    results.db
    results.db.lock
    ft_results/
      result_ft_....json`;

const query = `python scripts/management/query_lp_db_results.py \\
  --dataset go-mf \\
  --model orthrus \\
  --metrics \\
  --all-metrics`;

const incomplete = `python scripts/management/query_lp_db_results.py --incomplete`;

const summarize = `python scripts/linear_probe/summarize_metrics.py \\
  --data go-mf \\
  --task multilabel \\
  --split_type homology \\
  --target target`;

const embeddings = `python scripts/management/manage_embeddings.py \\
  --model orthrus \\
  --stats`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Results and analysis"
  description="Find persisted outputs, query run metadata, combine seeds, and interpret each metric."
  section="Run"
>
  <h2>Storage layout</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={storage} language="text" />
  <p>
    Pooled embeddings use compressed NPZ files with an
    <code>embedding</code> key. Ragged token embeddings use an HDF5
    <code>embeddings</code> group. Half-precision tensors are converted to
    float32 before they are saved.
  </p>

  <h2>Query linear-probe results</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={query} language="shell" />
  <p>
    Each <code>results.db</code> row records the model, task, target, split,
    seed, metrics, and creation time. Rerunning the same model, task, target,
    split, and seed replaces that row.
  </p>
  <Callout tone="important" label="Result identity">
    <p>
      The database key does not include split ratios or
      <code>eval_all_splits</code>. Runs that differ only in those settings can
      replace one another. Keep those settings fixed for one result database or
      use separate dataset output paths.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h3>Find incomplete seeded runs</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={incomplete} language="shell" />

  <h3>Combine completed seeds</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={summarize} language="shell" />
  <p>
    The summary writes an <code>all</code> seed row containing the mean and a
    95% interval computed as 1.96 times the standard error.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="important" label="Evaluation split">
    <p>
      <code>LinearProbeBuilder</code> evaluates validation data by default.
      The repository benchmark scripts set <code>eval_all_splits=True</code>
      and can write train, validation, and test metrics. Check the stored split
      before comparing values.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Metric reference</h2>
  <table tabindex="0" aria-label="Metric reference">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Task</th><th>Metrics written by the package</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Regression</td><td>MSE, Pearson r, Spearman rho (stored under the legacy key <code>p</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Binary classification</td><td>MCC, balanced accuracy, AUROC, AUPRC</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Multiclass</td><td>MCC, balanced accuracy, accuracy, macro F1, micro/macro AUROC and AUPRC</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Multilabel</td><td>Micro MCC and micro/macro AUROC and AUPRC</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Zero-shot variant-effect classification</td><td>AUROC and AUPRC</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Inspect embedding inventory</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={embeddings} language="shell" />
  <p>
    Use this before scheduling probes to check which model and dataset
    combinations are already present and how much storage they use.
  </p>

  <h2>Paper-specific aggregation</h2>
  <p>
    Paper figure scripts include publication-specific exclusions, renames, seed
    expectations, and baseline choices. Treat them as paper reproduction code,
    not as the general result API. The website leaderboard has its own
    documented normalization step so a new parquet snapshot can be validated
    before it is shown.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
